WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.360
Eleven machines.

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:03.663
Thirty-eight kilometres under the sea.

00:00:03.673 --> 00:00:06.104
Up front, a spinning cutter head grinds

00:00:06.114 --> 00:00:07.419
through chalk marl.

00:00:07.429 --> 00:00:09.119
Behind it, the walls go up:

00:00:09.129 --> 00:00:11.681
concrete segments, ring after ring.

00:00:11.691 --> 00:00:13.668
Some machines were as long as two

00:00:13.678 --> 00:00:15.052
football fields.

00:00:15.062 --> 00:00:16.012
Three tunnels:

00:00:16.022 --> 00:00:18.264
two for trains, one for service.

00:00:18.274 --> 00:00:20.835
In 1990, the two sides met.

00:00:20.845 --> 00:00:22.198
The British machines?

00:00:22.208 --> 00:00:24.770
Driven down, and buried under the sea.
